        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "`nvim_open_win()` has an `external` flag which does that. If we did that for all windows, then window-navigation commands (`c-w`) would need to be delegated to the UI. And my first thought is that seems to change the role of the UI in a way that isn't too useful",
            "created_at": "2026-07-01T17:23:36Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/38086#issuecomment-4858298907",
            "id": 4858298907,
